n.","The Mysteries of the Horizon"],"663481":["Golconda is an oil painting on canvas by Belgian surrealist René Magritte, painted in 1953. It is housed at the Menil Collection in Houston, Texas.","Golconda (Magritte)"],"1061035":["The Treachery of Images is a 1929 painting by Belgian surrealist painter René Magritte. It is also known as This Is Not a Pipe, Ceci n'est pas une pipe and The Wind and the Song.","The Treachery of Images"],"1151384":["The Son of Man is a 1964 painting by the Belgian surrealist painter René Magritte. It is perhaps his best-known artwork.","The Son of Man"],"1923232":["The Castle of the Pyrenees is an oil-on-canvas painting by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte, completed in 1959. It is held at the Israel Museum, in Jerusalem.","The Castle of the Pyrenees"],"2022606":["Not to Be Reproduced is an oil on canvas painting by the Belgian surrealist artist René Magritte, from 1937. It is held by the Museum Boijmans Van Beuningen, in Rotterdam.","Not to Be Reproduced"],"2571851":["Elective Affinities is a 1933 painting by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte. The title is taken from Johann Wolfgang von Goethe's 1809 novel Elective Affinities.","Elective Affinities (painting)"],"2600695":["The Empire of Light is the title of a succession of paintings by René Magritte. They depict the paradoxical image of a nocturnal landscape beneath a sunlit sky.","The Empire of Light"],"2918824":["The Portrait is an oil on canvas painting by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte, from 1935.","The Portrait (Magritte)"],"3230453":["The Lovers is a surrealist painting by René Magritte, made in Paris in 1928. It is the first in a series of four variations, depicting two people kissing passionately with each of their faces covered in a white cloth.","The Lovers (Magritte)"],"3818801":["The Menaced Assassin is a 1927 oil-on-canvas painting by Belgian surrealist artist René Magritte. It is held at the Museum of Modern Art, in New York.","The Menaced Assassin"],"7730158":["The Difficult Crossing (La traversée difficile) is the name given to two oil-on-canvas paintings by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte. The original version was completed in 1926 during Magritte's early prolific years of surrealism and is currently held in a private collection.","The Difficult Crossing"],"7731980":["The Empty Mask is an oil on canvas painting by Belgian surrealist painter René Magritte, from 1928. The painting was purchased in 1973 and is on display in the National Museum of Wales, in Cardiff.","The Empty Mask"],"7747550":["The Listening Room is an oil on canvas painting by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte which is currently part of the Menil Collection in Houston, Texas. A later version of the painting was made in 1958 and is held in a private collection.","The Listening Room"],"7750821":["The Meaning of Night is a painting by the Belgian Surrealist René Magritte. Painted in 1927, it is an oil painting on canvas with dimensions 139 cm by 105 cm and is in the Menil Collection, Houston.","The Meaning of Night (painting)"],"7763206":["The Seducer is a surrealist painting by René Magritte. It was created in 1950 and again in 1953 in Brussels, Belgium.","The Seducer"],"7805163":["Time Transfixed is a 1938 oil on canvas painting by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte. It is part of the permanent collection of the Art Institute of Chicago and is usually on display in the museum's Modern Wing.","Time Transfixed"],"12797191":["On the Threshold of Liberty refers to two oil on canvas paintings by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte. The work depicts a large room with the walls paneled with different scenes or windows.","On the Threshold of Liberty"],"15355687":["The Telescope is a 1963 oil on canvas painting by René Magritte.","The Telescope (Magritte)"],"15877654":["The Enchanted Pose was a 1927 painting by René Magritte depicting a side-by-side pair of identical female nudes in a bare interior. It has been lost since the 1930s.","The Enchanted Pose"],"19882741":["The Voice of Space is an oil painting by René Magritte. Four oil versions exist of the image.","The Voice of Space"],"19883989":["The False Mirror is a surrealist oil on canvas painting by René Magritte, from 1929. It depicts a human eye framing a cloudy, blue sky.","The False Mirror"],"19897946":["The Adulation of Space is an oil on canvas painting by Belgian surrealist artist René Magritte, created in 1927–1928. It is held in a private collection.","The Adulation of Space"],"19897977":["The Palace of Memories is an oil on canvas painting created by Belgian surrealist artist René Magritte, from 1939. It is held in a private collection.","The Palace of Memories"],"22043538":["16th September is a 1956 painting by Belgian surrealist painter René Magritte. It is now in the Royal Museum of Fine Arts, Antwerp, which bought it directly from the artist.","16th September (painting)"],"33315651":["The Alarm Clock is an oil-on-canvas painting by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte, completed in 1957. It is held at a private collection.","The Alarm Clock (painting)"],"52707506":["The Human Condition is the title of four paintings by the Belgian surrealist René Magritte. One was completed in 1933 and is in the collection of the National Gallery of Art in Washington, D.C. Another one was completed in 1935 and is part of the Simon Spierer Collection in Geneva, Switzerland.","The Human Condition (Magritte)"],"60323977":["The Good Example is a 1953 oil on canvas painting by René Magritte, part of the collection of the Musée National d'Art Moderne in Paris but stored and displayed at the Museum of Grenoble since 28 April 2004. It is a standing portrait of the art dealer Alexandre Iolas, holding an umbrella.","The Good Example"],"60683811":["The Secret Player is a 1927 painting by Belgian surrealist artist René Magritte. This surreal oil on canvas mainly depicts two baseball players at the foot of giant bowling pins and under a black leatherback turtle floating in the air.","The Secret Player"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}